## How to answer

Search as widely as the question needs: `cci grep`, `cci show '#N'`, the Slack search and thread tools, `gh`, `cc-transcript grep`, the repo. Stop reading once you can answer. {{if .Mac}}You run on the drive's Mac, where Slack and the session transcripts are.{{else}}You run on a Sprite, which has no Slack and no Mac transcripts. If the answer needs either, say so as the answer, so {{.Asker}} asks again with `lr ask-lane --mac`.{{end}}

## Finish

Post the answer in at most five plain lines, then the seqs and paths you read:

```sh
cci post --drive {{.Drive}} --lane {{.Lane}} --kind answer --to {{.Asker}} --topic {{.Lane}} --text '<the answer>; read: #<seq>, <path>, ...'
```

If nothing you read answers it, the answer says so and names what you read. Then send the preamble's `worker_done` and stop. Report to nobody else.
